.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    See how last finalized overall ratings line up with the assignment-energy rule of thumb... a calibration view, not a verdict on managers.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  %p.mb-2
    With MAAP, a huge advantage is that we encourage
    %strong specificity.
    Specificity leads to more alignment on what is important, and therefore better coaching, and therefore a workforce that is continuously improving in the most impactful ways. Not to mention it vastly increases fairness.
  %p.mb-3
    Guidance on this matrix uses the same in-flight / official energy mix as the position check-in tip. Values and non-assignment work are not in the formula, so divergence can be intentional and healthy. Nobody ever sees their own marker.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  %ul.mb-3
    %li X-axis is the actual last finalized overall rating (six statuses, worst on the left).
    %li Y-axis is guidance only: Developing, Accomplished, or Exceptional (best at the top).
    %li More than 20% working-to-meet energy → Developing. More than 50% exceeding with none working-to-meet → Exceptional. Otherwise Accomplished.
    %li Filters are shared with MgrStance+Rating Matrix. People missing an actual rating or computable guidance are listed under the grid.

  %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 What a cell might mean
  %p.small.text-muted.mb-2
    These are conversation starters, not labels to put on people. Use them to ask better questions. Example names match the sample matrix below.
  .table-responsive.mb-3
    %table.table.table-bordered.table-sm.mb-0.small
      %thead
        %tr
          %th Pattern
          %th Example
          %th Guidance (Y)
          %th Actual overall (X)
          %th What to explore
      %tbody
        %tr
          %td
            %strong High impact, hard to coach
          %td Blake
          %td Exceptional
          %td Developing or below
          %td
            Assignment energy says they are exceeding where it counts, but the overall rating is low. Often strong outcomes paired with trust, collaboration, or consistency gaps... or a rating that is lagging the work.
        %tr
          %td
            %strong Likely under-credited
          %td Nina
          %td Exceptional
          %td Accomplished
          %td
            Guidance says Exceptional and the overall landed Accomplished. They may have been "robbed" of the top box... or a critical assignment is missing from the energy picture.
        %tr
          %td
            %strong Quiet over-delivery
          %td Elena, Quinn
          %td Developing or Accomplished
          %td Exceptional
          %td
            Overall is Exceptional while assignment-energy guidance is lower. They may be exceeding on the right assignments even when those are not "big" by energy... or the manager is being too easy.
        %tr
          %td
            %strong Aligned
          %td Maya, Casey, Riley
          %td Same band as actual
          %td Same band as guidance
          %td
            Energy mix and overall rating tell a consistent story. Still coach... but you are not fighting a mismatch first.

